## 13. Firestore Security Rules

File: `firestore.rules`

The rules implement a role-based access model with helper functions such as `isAdmin()`, `isSuperAdmin()`, `isEditor()`, and `isSupport()`.

Key access rules include:

- `properties`: readable by published listings or admin/editor/support roles
- `sellerSubmissions`: writable only by valid submissions and admin review workflows
- `inquiries`: readable and writable in authorized admin contexts
- `users`: user can access own profile; admin can read all users
- `siteSettings` and `websiteContent`: public read; admin write access
- `adminLogs`: admin-only read/write restrictions
- `admins`: `allow write: if false;` meaning Admin SDK writes are expected there, not client-side writes

### Example from `firestore.rules`

```firestore
function isAdmin() {
  return isSignedIn() && (
    request.auth.token.admin == true ||
    request.auth.token.superAdmin == true ||
    request.auth.token.role == 'admin' ||
    request.auth.token.role == 'super_admin' ||
    request.auth.token.role == 'super-admin' ||
    exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/admins/$(request.auth.uid))
  );
}

match /properties/{id} {
  allow read: if resource.data.published == true || canReadAdminData();
  allow create: if canManageListings() && hasValidPropertyStatus(request.resource.data) && (
    ...
  );
}
```

