## 16. Storage Security Rules

File: `storage.rules`

The rules enforce allowed public access and admin-only editing for uploads.

Example from file:

```firestore
match /properties/{allPaths=**} {
  allow read: if true;
  allow write: if (isAdmin() || isEditor()) && isImage();
  allow delete: if isAdmin();
}

match /sellerSubmissions/{allPaths=**} {
  allow get: if true;
  allow create: if isImage();
  allow list: if false;
  allow update, delete: if isAdmin();
}
```

Rules also validate:

- image size <= 5 MB
- image MIME type must be `image/(jpeg|png|webp)`
- Admin/editor permissions are checked using Firebase auth token claims

Status: Implemented and verified.

